        {
          "id": 1574987925,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Iperf2 packets don't have a field that tells how many bytes the header(s) take. Therefore the two pass approach is used: first pass is needed to determine the length of headers, then, depending on the tvb len, we either move on to the 2nd pass and call header subdissectors, or ask TCP for more data.\nFlags are not *set* by the dissector code, flags are *read* from the packet fields.\nTo summarize, I don't see a problem with the current logic - the code works fine with all PCAPs I have in possession. If it doesn't work with some PCAPs - please share them, so the code can be fixed.",
          "author": {
            "id": 7405680,
            "username": "tulup1",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Andrii Vladyka",
            "state": "active",
